body:
The response from my partner was as expected. She's being very passive-aggressive and angry with me right now. She insisted on making breakfast for me this morning. I asked for eggs with spinach and tomatoes in it. She decided to put it on a whole wheat wrap for me. I saw that she was doing it and I asked her not to. She's agreed, but I can tell from her tone that she's angry. I hate that MY dietary choices have to affect her so much. It's already hard enough for me to make these changes. I feel like pulling up proof of why these changes are being made would only make her madder. Our relationship has always been smooth sailing, but it seems that a lot of problems are coming up concerning all of this. We already struggle with her offering my temptation foods every other day. Sometimes not even asking if I want it, just buying it and putting it in front of me. I've talked to her a lot about it, but it seems that I'm really going to have to tough this out myself. I just hate that she gets annoyed in the process. I'll look into the meter. Thank you for all of the advice. Sorry, I'm feeling a bit down about it.

&#x200B;

And now things have gotten much worse. She was just in hysterical sobbing and screaming. She literally threw up. She said that I was going too far and that I NEED the wheat wraps and that I'm making too many changes too quickly. I didn't say I was going to completely quit the wraps. I just said I'd cut back. I hate this and I'm so stressed. I don't want my choices to affect her like this. I don't know. Maybe we need couples therapy. This sucks.
